WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.040
To learn what a protein does, you lower it or remove it.

2
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.460
A knockout alters the DNA.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.440
A knockdown lowers how much protein a gene makes and leaves the gene intact.

4
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.380
Before double-stranded RNA was understood, worm biologists silenced genes by

5
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.480
injecting antisense RNA, with sense RNA as the control.

6
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.200
In some experiments, the sense RNA silenced the gene too.

7
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:39.433
Fire, Mello and colleagues injected double-stranded RNA into the worm C. elegans.

8
00:00:40.053 --> 00:00:43.353
It was substantially more effective than either single strand.

9
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:49.593
Only a few molecules were needed per affected cell, which suggested a catalytic or

10
00:00:49.593 --> 00:00:56.473
amplifying step. Montgomery, Xu and Fire found no evidence of change in the DNA

11
00:00:56.473 --> 00:01:00.753
sequence. Their data supported messenger RNA as the target.

12
00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:06.087
An enzyme called Dicer cuts double-stranded RNA.

13
00:01:07.147 --> 00:01:13.007
Pieces 21 and 22 nucleotides long were identified as the sequence-specific

14
00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:18.847
mediators. We call them small interfering RNA, or siRNA.

15
00:01:19.827 --> 00:01:25.387
A complex called RISC holds the siRNA with Argonaute-family proteins.

16
00:01:26.287 --> 00:01:29.767
The siRNA pairs with matching messenger RNA.

17
00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:33.967
In mammalian cells, Argonaute2 supplies the cutting.

18
00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.447
The messenger RNA is cut, and the gene makes less protein.

19
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:46.407
In many mammalian cells, long double-stranded RNA sets off broad antiviral

20
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:52.587
responses. So researchers used short synthetic siRNA duplexes.

21
00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:59.687
An shRNA is a hairpin, usually transcribed inside the cell from an RNA polymerase

22
00:01:59.687 --> 00:02:06.767
III promoter. A morpholino binds its target RNA and prevents translation or splicing.

23
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.040
Check the knockdown: transcript by quantitative RT-PCR.

24
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.200
Protein by Western analysis.

25
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:23.420
An idealised example: An siRNA lowers protein X by 80 percent on a blot, and cells migrate

26
00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.060
more slowly. That is an association.

27
00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.160
It does not show that X is dispensable or essential.

28
00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.633
Two things mislead.

29
00:02:33.473 --> 00:02:40.293
An siRNA can hit other genes: in HeLa profiling, the most enriched off-target six

30
00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:45.273
nucleotide sequence was complementary to positions two to seven of the guide.

31
00:02:46.113 --> 00:02:52.513
And morpholino mistargeting could induce p53-dependent neural cell death in zebrafish embryos.

32
00:02:53.453 --> 00:02:55.293
Three controls catch this.

33
00:02:55.793 --> 00:02:57.333
Measure the target protein.

34
00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:01.613
Use two non-overlapping reagents against one gene.

35
00:03:02.693 --> 00:03:07.073
Rescue with a transgene made resistant by silent changes in the target site.

36
00:03:08.073 --> 00:03:14.013
Even a good rescue does not formally exclude a phenotype that also needs an off-target effect.

37
00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:16.547
The method was the finding.

38
00:03:17.487 --> 00:03:24.227
In 1998, Fire, Mello and colleagues showed that double-stranded RNA silences

39
00:03:24.227 --> 00:03:26.387
matching genes in C. elegans.

40
00:03:27.287 --> 00:03:32.387
Fire and Mello shared the 2006 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine.

41
00:03:33.447 --> 00:03:40.407
In 2010, Coste, Patapoutian and colleagues knocked down candidate genes with siRNA

42
00:03:40.407 --> 00:03:46.187
in a mouse cell line and found Piezo1 required for mechanically activated current.

43
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:54.450
In 2007, Taneyhill, Coles and Bronner-Fraser blocked Snail2 translation with

44
00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.930
morpholinos, and cadherin6B was derepressed within 30 minutes.

45
00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:08.650
In 2005, Royle, Bright and Lagnado depleted clathrin by RNAi, and mitosis was

46
00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:15.230
prolonged. Clathrin triskelia rescued normal mitosis; the N-terminal domain did

47
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.310
not. A knockdown phenotype is an association with reduced protein.
